[18.043788, "o", "===== input/clarification.md =====\r\n"]
[18.048309, "o", "# Clarification — the client's later message\r\r\n\r\r\nWhat the client added afterwards, one entry per subject. The subject shown on each entry is the value the draft's `subject` column uses; any subject missing here is one the clarification leaves alone.\r\r\n\r\r\n## CL-301 `addressee`\r\r\n\r\r\nTo be clear: Adam is the father. The letter goes to Catherine's attorney — the mother's attorney — not to Adam's.\r\r\n\r\r\n## CL-302 `request`\r\r\n\r\r\nThe request stands: neither child overnight in her care unless the father is present.\r\r\n\r\r\n## CL-303 `enclosure`\r\r\n\r\r\nYes, enclose the certified copy of the custodial plan.\r\r\n\r\r\n"]
[18.04876, "o", "## CL-304 `salutation`\r\r\n\r\r\nOpen with Dear Counsel, since the attorney's name is still to be confirmed.\r\r\n\r\r\n## CL-305 `copies`\r\r\n\r\r\nDo not copy anyone on it.\r\r\n\r\r\n## CL-306 `delivery`\r\r\n\r\r\nSend it by post to counsel's office.\r\r\n\r\r\n## CL-307 `tone`\r\r\n\r\r\nUse a firm, formal and brief tone — not soft, and not long-winded.\r\r\n\r\r\n## CL-308 `behavioural_plan`\r\r\n\r\r\nThe plan is about confidence, stability and peer relations. The stays have set back confidence only — not the whole plan.\r\r\n\r\r\n## CL-309 `concern`\r\r\n\r\r\nI am concerned only about the position she has been put in. Do not raise whether she appreciates that the stays violate the order.\r\r\n"]
[18.049244, "o", "\r\n===== input/letter_lines.csv ====="]
[18.049568, "o", "\r\n"]
[18.055284, "o", "line_id,subject,position,cited_entry,wording\r\r\nST-101,right_of_first_refusal,agreed by the father,OI-202,\"Mr Adler agreed to a right of first refusal, so the children are not to be left overnight without him present.\"\r\r\nST-102,children_named,\"both children, with their ages\",OI-203,\"This concerns Noor, aged seven, and Imogen, aged twelve.\"\r\r\nST-103,overnight_stays,several occasions at her home or with a sitter,OI-204,On several occasions both children have stayed overnight at Ms Corwin's home or with a sitter while Mr Adler was away.\r\r\nST-104,addressee,the father's attorney,OI-201,To counsel for Mr Adler.\r\r\nST-105,inconsistent_accounts,\"wife to the school, resident to clinicians, sitter to the sender\",OI-205,\"Mr Adler has described Ms Corwin as his wife to the school, as the person Imogen lives with to her clinicians, and as a babysitter to me.\"\r\r\nST-106,concern,violation limb only,OI-206,I am concerned that Ms Corwin may not appreciate that these stays violate the custodial order.\r\r\nST-107,behavioural_plan,th"]
[18.055633, "o", "e stays have had no effect on the plan,OI-207,\"Imogen's behavioural plan focuses on her confidence and stability, and the stays have not affected her progress.\"\r\r\nST-108,request,no overnight stays in her care unless the father is present,CL-302,I ask that neither child remain overnight in Ms Corwin's care unless Mr Adler is present.\r\r\nST-109,enclosure,a certified copy of the custodial plan,OI-209,A certified copy of the custodial plan is enclosed.\r\r\nST-110,tone,firm and detailed,OI-210,I set out the position firmly and in full detail below.\r\r\nST-111,sender_signature,the sender's own name,OI-211,\"Yours sincerely, Delphine Marr.\"\r\r\nST-112,salutation,Dear Counsel,CL-304,\"Dear Counsel,\"\r\r\nST-113,copies,copied to the father,CL-305,Copy: Mr Adler.\r\r\nST-114,reply_deadline,a reply within seven days,OI-299,I would be grateful for a reply within seven days.\r\r\nST-115,school_reference,the school principal named,OI-298,\"The school principal, Ms Oduya, can confirm the account given to the school.\"\r\r\nST-116,mediation_offer,"]
